### 5.1 Preprocessor ([preprocessor.py](file:///c:/Users/JapanKachhiya/ADIVA-Automated-Data-Intelligence-and-Validation-Agent/backend/extractors/preprocessor.py))

- **File type detection** — extension + magic bytes (libmagic if available)
- **Quality assessment** — readability score 0-1, page count, scanned vs digital detection
- **Scanned PDF detection** — checks text-to-page ratio: if digital PDF has very little text, it's treated as scanned
- **Page splitting** — splits multi-page PDFs for per-page processing

### 5.2 Extractors

| Extractor | File | Input | Key Features |
|-----------|------|-------|--------------|
| [PDFExtractor](file:///c:/Users/JapanKachhiya/ADIVA-Automated-Data-Intelligence-and-Validation-Agent/backend/extractors/pdf_extractor.py) | `pdf_extractor.py` | Digital PDFs | 3-backend table extraction (pdfplumber → camelot → tabula), deduplication |
| [OCRExtractor](file:///c:/Users/JapanKachhiya/ADIVA-Automated-Data-Intelligence-and-Validation-Agent/backend/extractors/ocr_extractor.py) | `ocr_extractor.py` | Scanned PDFs, Images | 2-tier OCR (Tesseract → EasyOCR fallback), auto-rotation, deskew, shadow removal, DPI detection, multi-script support (English/Hindi/Gujarati) |
| [DOCXExtractor](file:///c:/Users/JapanKachhiya/ADIVA-Automated-Data-Intelligence-and-Validation-Agent/backend/extractors/docx_extractor.py) | `docx_extractor.py` | Word .docx | Merged cell detection, table structure analysis, paragraph extraction |

### 5.3 AI Agent ([ai_agent.py](file:///c:/Users/JapanKachhiya/ADIVA-Automated-Data-Intelligence-and-Validation-Agent/backend/ai_agent.py))

The LLM brain of ADIVA. Uses **Mistral AI** for two critical tasks:

**1. Document Classification** (`classify_document`)
- Sends a 2000-char text sample to Mistral
- Returns one of 21 document types + confidence score + reasoning
- Example: `{type: "resume", confidence: 0.99, reasoning: "..."}`

**2. Structured Data Extraction** (`extract_structured_data`)
- Looks up the matching schema from `SCHEMA_REGISTRY` (e.g., `ResumeSchema`)
- Builds a structured prompt with the schema definition + extraction instructions
- For **long documents (>8000 chars)**: uses **chunked extraction** with overlap, then merges results
- Merge rule: later chunks fill in `null` fields, lists are extended (not replaced)
- Parses JSON from LLM response (handles markdown fences, partial JSON)

